## Summary
The article discusses differences in how countries evaluate the performance of high-salary CEOs. Korea focuses on a 3-year performance period, while the US and UK consider longer timeframes of 5 to 10 years. This comparison highlights variations in corporate governance practices across regions.

## Key Points
- Korea evaluates CEO performance over a 3-year period.
- The US and UK use longer evaluation periods of 5 to 10 years.
- This difference may affect CEO compensation, incentives, and corporate strategies.
- The variation could stem from cultural or regulatory factors in business environments.


